# A message that names us as a whole word, under the server's casemap, is a
# highlight; one where our nick is part of a longer word is not, and our
# own lines never are. Only what others say counts as unread: not events,
# not our own echoes, never the console.
= nick tex[]
! welcome echo-message
< :tex[]!u@h JOIN #c
> MODE #c
? unread #c 0 highlights 0
< :bob!b@h PRIVMSG #c :hey TEX{}: look
? unread #c 1 highlights 1
< :bob!b@h PRIVMSG #c :tex[]s are cool
< :bob!b@h PRIVMSG #c :xtex[] no
? unread #c 3 highlights 1
< :bob!b@h NOTICE #c :(tex[]) notice
? unread #c 4 highlights 2
< :tex[]!u@h PRIVMSG #c :tex[] talking to myself
< :carol!c@h JOIN #c
? unread #c 4 highlights 2
< :bob!b@h PRIVMSG tex[] :private, tex[]
? unread bob 1 highlights 1
< :irc.test NOTICE tex[] :tex[] from the server
? unread console 0 highlights 0
? registered tex[]
